摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Windows desktop automation for DeepSeek Harness: the in-box MCP client bridge mounted against CursorTouch/Windows-MCP, with an off-by-default Computer Use switch and an in-app dependency installer.","id":"gh:1413849053","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-windows-mcp","slug":"helloHub1212/dsh-windows-mcp","topics":["computer-use","deepseek-harness","desktop-automation","dsh","dsh-plugin","mcp","windows","windows-mcp"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Windows desktop automation for DeepSeek Harness: the in-box MCP client bridge mounted against Cursor"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"Touch/Windows-MCP, with an off-by-default Computer Use switch and an in-app dependency installer."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-windows-mcp"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** · 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Windows desktop automation for DeepSeek Harness** — lets the DSH agent see your screen and drive y"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ws desktop automation for DeepSeek Harness** — lets the DSH agent see your screen and drive your PC."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This plugin connects CursorTouch/Windows-MCP to DSH by mounting one loader row against the **MCP cli"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ent bridge that already ships inside DeepSeek Harness**. There is no reimplemented protocol client a"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"nd no second copy of the MCP SDK: the plugin is a *carrier bundle*, and everything you can do comes "},{"id":"p5s4","text":"from the official bridge."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## What it gives the agent"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"With the plugin installed and Windows-MCP reachable, these tools appear in the tool list:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Tool | What it does |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| `mcp__windows__Screenshot` | Capture the screen; the image lands in the conversation as a real att"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"achment |\n| `mcp__windows__Snapshot` | Capture an accessibility tree (text, no image tokens) |\n| `mc"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"p__windows__DisplayInventory` | Enumerate displays and their geometry |\n| `mcp__windows__Click` / `M"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"ove` / `Scroll` | Mouse input |\n| `mcp__windows__Type` / `Shortcut` | Keyboard input |\n| `mcp__windo"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"ws__Wait` / `WaitFor` | Sleep, or wait until a UI condition holds |\n| `mcp__windows__Scrape` | Extra"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"ct text from a window |\n| `mcp__windows__MultiSelect` / `MultiEdit` | Batch element selection / batc"},{"id":"p10s7","text":"h edits |\n| `mcp__windows__Clipboard` | Read and write the clipboard |\n| `mcp__windows__Process` | L"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"ist, start and stop processes |\n| `mcp__windows__Notification` | Read notifications |\n| `mcp__window"},{"id":"p10s9","text":"s__Registry` | Read and write registry values |\n| `mcp__windows__ControlStatus` | Control-loop state"},{"id":"p10s10","text":". **Cannot be disabled** — upstream force-keeps it |\n| `mcp__windows__App` | Launch/switch apps. *Ex"},{"id":"p10s11","text":"cluded by default* (upstream only supports it reliably on an English Windows install) |\n| `mcp__wind"},{"id":"p10s12","text":"ows__PowerShell` / `FileSystem` | *Excluded by default* — DSH already ships shell and file tools |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Plus one tool of its own, `windows_mcp_doctor`, which explains what is wrong when the `mcp__windows_"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"_*` tools are missing."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The composer also gains a **Computer Use** pill, next to the permission control: it shows how many d"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"esktop tools are actually registered and remembers your choice across restarts (state file: `~/.dsh/"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"dsh-windows-mcp.state.json`). It starts **off** — a fresh install never hands the agent your desktop"},{"id":"p12s4","text":" until you switch the pill on yourself."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"- **Windows 10/11.**\n- **DeepSeek Harness Desktop** with the in-box `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` br"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"idge (0.2.0-rc.2 or newer).\n- **uv** on the `PATH` of the process that runs DSH — **Settings → Deskt"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"op** uses it to install Windows-MCP. DSH itself boots without it. `%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin` is sear"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"ched even when it is not on `PATH`.\n- **A model that accepts image input** if you want the agent to "},{"id":"p15s5","text":"actually *see* screenshots."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Boot is never blocked by the dependency"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The bridge row ships **disabled**, on purpose. A `uvx`-style first launch\nresolves Windows-MCP's Pyt"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"hon dependencies from the package index, and on a slow\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"This plugin hands the model your mouse, your keyboard, your clipboard, your\nprocesses and your regis"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"try. Treat installing it as handing over control of the\ndesktop session it runs in."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"What the design does and does not do:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- **No network exposure by default.** The default row is stdio: a child process\nconnected by pipes, "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"not a listening socket.\n- **Secret hygiene on the child process.** The bridge starts MCP children fr"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"om a\nscrubbed environment: variable names matching `KEY|PASSWORD|SECRET|TOKEN` and\n**all** `DSH_*` v"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"ariables are removed before the configured `env` is merged in.\nCredentials should therefore be passe"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"d explicitly through the row's `env`, not\ninherited.\n- **No telemetry from this plugin.** Upstream's"},{"id":"p21s6","text":" own PostHog reporting is\nexplicitly disabled in the shipped defaults.\n- **Remote serving is upstrea"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"m's problem, not a hidden default.** If you switch\nto HTTP, upstream enforces loopback host filterin"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"g and refuses to start on a\nnon-loopback address without an auth key.\n- **Switch flips are a window "},{"id":"p21s9","text":"decision, not a network one.** Every mutating\nroute (`/state`, `/prepare`, `/prepare/cancel`, `/brid"},{"id":"p21s10","text":"ge`, `/update`,\n`/settings`) requires the signed session cookie the DSH window receives during\nthe l"},{"id":"p21s11","text":"aunch-token exchange; without it the request is refused with `401`. A\nscript, `curl`, or a model wit"},{"id":"p21s12","text":"h shell access cannot turn desktop control on for\nitself. Reads stay open so pages can render before"},{"id":"p21s13","text":" anything is decided.\n- **When the cookie cannot be checked, the plugin says so.** A composition tha"},{"id":"p21s14","text":"t\nmounts no `connection` service (headless hosts, Electron `file://`) cannot be\nauthenticated; `/sta"},{"id":"p21s15","text":"te` then reports `\"gate\": {\"cookie\": \"unobservable\"}`. In\nthat case do not expose the web server on "},{"id":"p21s16","text":"a non-loopback `--host`.\n- **Files are still files.** The Computer Use flag in\n`$DSH_HOME/dsh-window"},{"id":"p21s17","text":"s-mcp.state.json` and the machine-written patch block are\nordinary files owned by the same user. An "},{"id":"p21s18","text":"agent that can write them can still\nchange the plugin's behaviour across a restart — the cookie gate"},{"id":"p21s19","text":" closes the\nHTTP path, not filesystem trust. If that matters to you, run the desktop on a\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness plugins are loader patches, and a patch row may mount a package\nthat lives inside t"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"he Electron `app.asar` — the loader resolves official\n`@deepseek-ai/*` names from the Desktop instal"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"l anchor. Third-party code cannot\n`import` those packages, but it *can* name them in a patch, becaus"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"e the mount\nhappens inside the loader rather than inside plugin code. That is the whole trick\nbehind"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"ppens inside the loader rather than inside plugin code. That is the whole trick\nbehind this package:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Consequences worth knowing:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- The integration is **version-sensitive** in one direction only: the bridge\nconfig schema belongs t"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"o DSH, not to this plugin. `package.json` declares the\npatch; DSH decides how to read it.\n- Image pr"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"ojection is a bridge feature: MCP image blocks are saved as DSH\nattachments and surfaced as native i"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"mage content. Audio and embedded resources\ndegrade to diagnostic text.\n- **MCP prompts are not suppo"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"rted** by the bridge (resources are, on demand)."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
